{
  "slug": "wiki-wonka",
  "name": "Wiki Wonka",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "wiki-wonka is an agent-driven system for building and maintaining a structured, evolving wiki of knowledge. Instead of relying on stateless retrieval (RAG) for every query, wiki-wonka compiles and curates knowledge into a persistent, interlinked set of Markdown pages. The LLM agent handles all the summarizing, cross-referencing, and bookkeeping—so your knowledge base compounds and improves over time.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills**, **1 agent** and **5 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `ingest` (Add new sources to the wiki, creating and updating pages as needed), `lint` (Scan the wiki for structural, factual, and navigational problems — and fix what you can, flag what you…), `query` (Answer questions by reading and synthesizing information from the wiki)\n- **Agents** (1): `wiki-wonka-orchestrator.agent` (wiki-wonka main agent)\n- **Hooks** (5): `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `FileChanged`, `SessionStart`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install wiki-wonka@claude-community` from `cooperacode/wiki-wonka`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 3,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 5
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
